      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "This paper details some of the patient's psychological factors with which each allied health professional must deal when interacting with an ill person. Successful professional/patient intervention is heavily dependent on a sensitivity to these factors. Within this framework, this paper deals with the personality dynamics which facilitate the effective rehabilitation of patients in general, but coronary heart disease patients in particular."},
